&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Artificial Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inizio may use AI technologies to support certain aspects of our recruitment process, but our human recruiting team makes all hiring decisions at Inizio. We are committed to fair, inclusive, and human-led hiring practices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who/What is Artefact?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Artefact is a next-generation strategy and data consulting firm dedicated to transforming&amp;nbsp;organizations through data and AI. We combine the rigor of top-tier strategy consulting&amp;nbsp;with deep expertise in data, digital, and analytics to help clients achieve tangible&lt;br&gt;business impact.&lt;br&gt;With 1,800+ consultants, data scientists, and engineers across 23 countries, we work&amp;nbsp;with global leaders such as Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange, and Sanofi. Our Zurich office is&amp;nbsp;at the heart of Artefact’s growth, advising clients on their most pressing strategic&amp;nbsp;challenges — from AI strategy and governance to digital transformation roadmaps and&amp;nbsp;new business model design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We are looking for a Senior Data &amp;amp; AI Architect who combines business strategy and technology across Data and GenAI. You will design the operating model and the organization of the Data &amp;amp; GenAI CoE, define the target architecture, and steer data products from demand through to rollout.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Operating model and organization&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design the Data &amp;amp; AI operating model (centralized, federated, hub-and-spoke) following Data Mesh principles: roles, responsibilities, domain ownership and governance mechanisms.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Define the organization of the Data &amp;amp; GenAI CoE: scope, service catalogue, skills, sizing and engagement model with business domains.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design end-to-end processes for demand management, use case prioritization, funding and value tracking.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Architecture and technology choices&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Define the target data platform architecture on cloud (Azure, AWS, GCP) and Databricks, including GenAI components (RAG, agents, vector stores, LLMOps).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Run make-or-buy analyses and vendor selections: scouting, evaluation criteria, business case, TCO and final recommendation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Check that architecture, security and data governance choices are consistent with enterprise standards and with the operating model.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Data products: from demand to rollout&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Gather and formalize functional requirements with the business, translating them into data products with owners, consumers, SLAs and quality metrics.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design data products from both a functional angle (use cases, KPIs, impacted processes) and a technical one (data model, pipelines, interfaces, serving layer).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Act as design authority during implementation: review system integrator solutions and oversee quality, progress and risks of the rollout.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At least 4 years of professional experience in IT.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At least 2 years on projects focused on AI/GenAI, Data Mesh and functional requirements gathering.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Consulting experience, ideally in strategy consulting, combined with experience at a system integrator or delivery firm.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Hands-on experience designing operating models, Data/AI organizations or CoEs.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience with make-or-buy analyses, vendor selection or target architecture definition.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Excellent written and spoken English.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Technical and functional skills:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You will not be expected to write code, but you need to know the technologies well enough to assess them, challenge vendors and spot a flawed setup.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Data Mesh and governance: domain ownership, data products, federated governance, data contracts, catalogues and lineage (e.g. Unity Catalog, OpenMetadata, Collibra).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cloud: data and AI PaaS services on at least one of Azure, AWS and GCP; security, networking and FinOps principles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Databricks: Lakehouse, Delta Lake, Unity Catalog, Workflows; ability to assess design and cost.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;GenAI: RAG and agentic architectures, LLMOps, model evaluation, platforms such as Azure AI Foundry, Vertex AI and Bedrock.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Operating model: Data/AI organization, CoE, roles (data owner, data steward, product owner), demand and portfolio processes.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Requirements and delivery: requirements gathering, user stories, process modelling, agile methods, programme governance.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Business: business cases, TCO, value tracking, and the ability to translate technical choices into economic impact.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;German not strictly required.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience with clients in pharma sector.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cloud or Databricks certifications (e.g. Azure Solutions Architect, Databricks Data Engineer or Solutions Architect).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience in tech due diligence or post-merger transformation projects.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Prior technical background as an engineer or developer.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A role bridging strategy and technology, with direct impact on client decisions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;International projects on Data Mesh, data platforms and GenAI.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Close collaboration with the Project Lead and a growth path towards programme leadership roles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Location and working model: (Hybrid) Zurich or Lausanne.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive compensation package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in &lt;strong&gt;Zürich&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don’t worry if you don’t meet all the criteria! We value motivation, pragmatic problem-solving, and potential above all else. We’d love to hear from you and learn more about your passion for driving the AI revolution.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Capgemini and Cambridge Consultants&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Cambridge Consultants (part of Capgemini Invent) develops breakthrough products, creates and licenses intellectual property, and provides business consultancy in technology-critical issues for clients worldwide. For more than 50 years, the company has been helping its clients turn business opportunities into commercial successes, whether they are launching first-to-market products, entering new markets, or expanding existing markets through the introduction of new technologies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Capgemini Group is a global leader in partnering with companies to transform and manage their business by harnessing the power of technology. The Group is guided every day by its purpose of unleashing human energy through technology for an inclusive and sustainable future. It is a responsible and diverse group of 340,000 team members in more than 50 countries, reporting 2025 Global revenues of €22.5 billion. With its strong 55+ year heritage, Capgemini is trusted by its clients to unlock the value of technology to address the entire breadth of their business needs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Role Description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Trusted AI and Secure Technologies (TASTE) group in Cambridge, UK provides advisory consulting and technical strategy and development for clients wishing to understand and leverage novel technologies for cybersecurity, AI assurance, post-quantum cryptography, and trusted digital-physical systems.&amp;nbsp; Our team provides technical consultancy in areas ranging from government policy to technology roadmaps, system architectures, testing, and post-quantum security migration for a wide range of clients, primarily in the critical national infrastructure and public sectors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are looking for a talented, experienced engineering project leader with an interest in assessing, designing and implementing trusted systems and architectures. Particular areas of focus we are looking for include post-quantum cryptography, security approaches for combined IT/OT systems, AI-enabled cybersecurity, cybersecurity for AI systems.&amp;nbsp; Main sectors of interest are government/public sector (including defence and security), energy and utilities, smart infrastructure, and mobility, but we are also active in other sectors including healthcare, consumer, and bioinnovation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In this role you will advise both CC clients and CC project teams on how to assess, design and develop appropriate security and assurance (both processes and technical approach) for both existing organisational networks and systems, and for novel applications, systems and devices.&amp;nbsp; This may involve both advisory work and actual design or development.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; A significant portion of time would be spent on leading client-facing work on post-quantum cryptography strategies, approaches and migration. There will also be opportunities to get involved in project bid development to provide technical advice on the feasibility and complexity of bids, and suggested solutions.&amp;nbsp; Some examples of recent work are linked below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;2&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cambridgeconsultants.com/quantum-tools-to-tackle-the-cybersecurity-threat-to-energy/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;Quantum tools to tackle the cybersecurity threat to energy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
