&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager on GitLab&#39;s Authentication team, you&#39;ll build and lead a team of engineers in Bangalore who own how users, applications, tokens, and artificial intelligence (AI) agents sign in to GitLab.&amp;nbsp;At GitLab, we see our team as our product. You&#39;ll need to be technically credible in authentication protocols such as OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect (OIDC), and Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML). Your main focus will be hiring well, growing your engineers, and helping the team deliver on commitments that other parts of GitLab depend on.&amp;nbsp;You&#39;ll guide your team&#39;s work on OAuth across Cells, global identities, token consolidation, and moving authentication out of the Ruby on Rails monolith onto GATE, GitLab&#39;s new authentication and authorization platform. You&#39;ll manage these multi-quarter programs with fixed deadlines and many dependent teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Hire, onboard, and grow a team of senior and intermediate engineers in Bangalore, working with talent acquisition during a high-volume hiring period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Own delivery for your team&#39;s part of the authentication roadmap: plan in milestones, track risks early, and communicate clearly when a date is at risk and what would change it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Work with your Staff Engineer and Product Manager to turn architecture decisions into shippable, feature-flagged increments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Protect your team&#39;s focus. Manage requests from other teams through one intake path, and make trade-offs visible to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Coordinate with the GATE Core, GATE Infra, Authorization, and Tenant Scale (Cells and Organizations) teams across India, Europe, and the Americas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Make sure the team runs what it builds, including on-call coverage, incident response for authentication issues, rate limits, and production readiness for new services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Build a team culture where security comes first, decisions are written down, and code review is thorough and kind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Give clear, regular feedback, run career conversations, and handle performance issues early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Take part in on-call or operational support where your team’s ownership model requires it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Significant experience as an engineering manager of backend or platform teams, including hiring and growing senior engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;A background as an engineer in identity, authentication, or security systems, with enough depth in OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SAML, and JSON Web Tokens to review designs and ask probing questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Experience delivering complex, multi-team programs against fixed dates, including migrations that must not disrupt existing customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Experience running production services, including on-call coverage, incident response, and reliability work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Working knowledge of Ruby on Rails or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Experience building a new team or growing one quickly while keeping the hiring bar high.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Clear, concise written English and comfort leading a team in an all-remote, asynchronous company across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re part of the Security Platform stage, alongside Authorization, GATE Core, GATE Infra, Secrets Manager, and other security teams. You&#39;ll partner closely with our existing Authentication engineers in Europe and the Americas.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Zscaler (NASDAQ: ZS) accelerates digital transformation so customers can be more agile, efficient, resilient, and secure. The Zscaler Zero Trust Exchange platform protects thousands of customers from cyberattacks and data loss by securely connecting users, devices, and applications in any location. Distributed across 200+ public data centers globally and thousands of private sites at the edge, the SASE-based Zero Trust Exchange is the world’s largest in-line cloud security platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the future of work is Human + AI and are building an AI-native enterprise where human potential is amplified by machine intelligence to solve the world’s hardest security challenges. Driven by deep customer obsession, we are committed to the mission, outcome, and to each other. We bring these commitments to life through three core behaviors: ownership and collaboration, trust through outcomes and impact, and a challenge culture with ongoing feedback. Ready to make an impact at the company pioneering security transformation in the AI era? Join us at Zscaler.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Staff DevOps Engineer, AI Security to join our team. This is a Remote role, reporting to the Director, DevOps - AI Security in the AI Guard department. This role owns and evolves the multi-region Kubernetes platform behind Zscaler’s AI Security products, which inspect LLM and agent traffic in real time using ML models on GPU infrastructure. As the senior platform engineer in EMEA, you will set technical direction for infrastructure, delivery, and tooling, and build the automation that lets a small team run a large, globally distributed fleet safely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own multi-region infrastructure and delivery, designing and maintaining OpenTofu/Terraform modules, CI/CD pipelines, Helm charts, and GitOps workflows to ensure repeatable, low-risk deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep EKS clusters healthy and cost-efficient across microservices, API gateways, Kafka-based event pipelines, and GPU model serving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build observability and automation into the platform by setting up metrics, logging, tracing, and SLOs while writing Python and Go tooling to reduce operational toil&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver secure and compliant infrastructure meeting CIS, STIG, and FedRAMP-style controls with hardened minimal images and least-privilege IAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the EMEA platform lead to improve incident response, mentor engineers, and partner globally on architecture and roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Success Profile)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in ambiguity. You&#39;re comfortable building the path as you walk it. You thrive in a dynamic environment, seeing ambiguity not as a hindrance, but as the raw material to build something meaningful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You act like an owner. Your passion for the mission fuels your bias for action. You operate with integrity because you genuinely care about the outcome. true ownership involves leveraging dynamic range: the ability to navigate seamlessly between high-level strategy and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a problem-solver. You love running towards the challenges because you are laser-focused on finding the solution, knowing that solving the hard problems delivers the biggest impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a high-trust collaborator. You are ambitious for the team, not just yourself. You embrace our challenge culture by giving and receiving ongoing feedback-knowing that candor delivered with clarity and respect is the truest form of teamwork and the fastest way to earn trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a learner. You have a true growth mindset and never stop developing yourself, actively seeking feedback to become a better partner and a stronger teammate. You love what you do and you do it with purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of AI/ML technologies and experience leveraging, securing, or positioning AI-driven solutions to optimize outcomes within your functional domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of engineering experience, including 5+ years in DevOps, SRE, or platform engineering with senior/staff-level ownership of production infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on AWS experience, including EKS, VPC networking, IAM, MSK, RDS/Aurora, Route 53, and load balancing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Terraform or OpenTofu experience, including module design and state management, plus CI/CD pipeline automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux fundamentals and Python and/or Go proficiency for automation, with experience running observability stacks and owning on-call, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out (Preferred Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in MLOps automation, including managing GPU workloads on Kubernetes, configuring model serving engines (Ray, KServe, Triton, or SageMaker), and building pipelines for LLM-based applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running multi-region, multi-tenant SaaS with cell-based architecture, Kafka event pipelines, ClickHouse analytical stores, and EU data residency boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of compliance frameworks (FedRAMP, CIS, STIG), hardened container images, and service mesh architectures like Istio or Envoy with mTLS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-REMOTE &lt;br&gt;#LI-MM8&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;At Zscaler, we are committed to building a team that reflects the communities we serve and the customers we work with. We foster an inclusive environment that values all backgrounds and perspectives, emphasizing collaboration and belonging. Join us in our mission to make doing business seamless and secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Benefits program is one of the most important ways we support our employees. Zscaler proudly offers comprehensive and inclusive benefits to meet the diverse needs of our employees and their families throughout their life stages, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;has-nudge&quot; data-nudge-id=&quot;5eb9419b-6a4d-4451-bfa6-e2eb96084be0&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Various health plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off plans for vacation and sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office perks, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;has-nudge&quot; data-nudge-id=&quot;5eb9419b-6a4d-4451-bfa6-e2eb96084be0&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Learn more about Zscaler&#39;s hybrid working model and benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zscaler.com/candidate-resource-hub&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this role, you adhere to applicable laws, regulations, and Zscaler policies, including those related to security and privacy standards and guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Zscaler is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all individuals. We strive to create a workplace where employees are treated with respect and have the chance to succeed. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy or related medical conditions), age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. &lt;em&gt;See more information by clicking on the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;link.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Transparency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler complies with all applicable federal, state, and local pay transparency rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler is committed to providing reasonable support (called accommodations or adjustments) in our recruiting processes for candidates who are differently abled, have long term conditions, mental health conditions or sincerely held religious beliefs, or who are neurodivergent or require pregnancy-related support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-intro-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section-inner&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Picnic, we&#39;re building the most secure milkman on earth. Our Security team owns the security tooling that protects Picnic, and we&#39;re looking for a Java Engineer to make it work everywhere: connecting our systems to those tools, automating checks across the whole company, and strengthening how we manage identity and access.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll be the engineer in the Security team. Instead of writing policies, you&#39;ll write the code that wires our security systems into the rest of Picnic, and you&#39;ll help product teams do the right thing by default.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of projects from concept to delivery, aligning technical solutions with business goals with a product engineering mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform work:&lt;/strong&gt; Own Picnic’s core Security and IAM platform services, and build integrations with internal and external services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity &amp;amp; Access:&lt;/strong&gt; Help take our IAM initiative from MVP to production. Look at the options, build or integrate the pieces and connect them to the systems Picnic runs on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with development teams to integrate security best practices into the software development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Ambassador: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct application security workshops to raise awareness and promote secure coding practices among developers.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech:&lt;/strong&gt; Java 21/25 (Spring 6 with Spring Boot 3.5, Reactor, Immutables, Maven), React, Angular, RabbitMQ, Kafka, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Git, Docker, AWS, Helm, Terraform, Kubernetes, Vault, Datadog, Python 3.x&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a Master’s Degree (in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Information Technology, Computer Engineering or a related technical field) or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 3-7 years of professional experience with Java.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine curiosity about security: experience isn’t required, but you’re excited to dive into topics like access control and to grow into the domain with us.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your English skills are on point (no Dutch required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re based in or happy to relocate to the Netherlands*&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For bonus points:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Security frameworks like NIST, CIS Controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience in IAM integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work from our office in Amsterdam. Being present makes a genuine difference to your team and the work. There&#39;s flexibility to work from home when needed, but if remote or hybrid-first is what you&#39;re after, this probably isn&#39;t the right fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✍🏼 Every expert was once a beginner!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including the Picnic Tech Academy, Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training. We also offer free professional weekly language courses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work in an awesome startup environment with the freedom to drive your own projects and create a visible impact. Our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🫱🏼‍🫲🏾 Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings to after-work drinks to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍎 You are what you eat&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get freshly prepared, healthy lunches and snacks (with plenty of vegetarian, vegan, and halal options). Coffee snob? Don’t worry, our amazing Picnic barista has you covered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚴🏽 Stay healthy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials. There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga, to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔋 Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self, as well as 25 vacation days per year, so you can recharge your batteries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌍 Benefits for expats&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It can be daunting starting a new job AND moving to a new country. That’s why we offer lots of support for our many expat colleagues, if you want to find our relocation benefits, see &lt;a href=&quot;https://jobs.picnic.app/en/relocation&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complexe projecten, volop mogelijkheden om te groeien en werken bij één van de top Microsoft system integrators van Nederland. Als Senior Project manager ben je verantwoordelijk voor de implementatie van Microsoft technologie en geef je leiding aan het projectteam van HSO.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We bouwen steeds vaker oplossingen voor klanten die niet alleen ERP willen, maar die bewust kiezen voor het Microsoft Cloud platform. En dus bijvoorbeeld ook kiezen voor Dynamics 365 for CRM, Field Service en Power BI. Omdat HSO één van de weinige Microsoft system integrators is, kunnen we klanten deze totaaloplossing bieden. De complexe en grotere internationale projecten vragen veel expertise en ervaring, Dus we hebben volop werk en uitdaging!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ben jij gewend om grootschalige Microsoft applicatie projecten te leiden?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wat ga je doen?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Als Senior Project manager schakel je continu tussen de belangen van de klant en HSO. De projecten zijn bovengemiddeld complex van aard en de stakeholders zijn vaak over meerdere bedrijven en de wereld verspreid. Dit is geen uitdaging maar gesneden koek voor jou.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jij beschikt over:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ten minste 5 jaar ervaring met ERP-implementaties als Project manager;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je deelt onze mind set: je bent een kritische denker, een ondernemende zelf starter en je verbindt je met het resultaat;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je business English is dik in orde, gezien onze internationale projecten;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je management vaardigheden zijn consulterend, anticiperend en voorstellend van aard en gebruikt deze eigenschappen om mensen met je mee te krijgen en effectief te laten functioneren;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ervaring met het Microsoft-platform, Dynamics AX 2012 of Dynamics 365 is een pre;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aantoonbare kennis van methodieken voor project management zowel waterval als Agile, bijvoorbeeld PRINCE II, PMI- of IPMA C/D-certificering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wat bieden we jou?   &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Werken bij HSO is uitdagend, we willen je daar graag een goede beloning voor teruggeven. Naast goede primaire voordelen bieden wij: &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Een competitief salaris en een jaarlijkse bonus op basis van bedrijfs-, team- en individuele prestaties&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobiliteitsvergoeding waarbij je of een auto kunt leasen of het bedrag toe kunt voegen aan je salaris. Daarbovenop krijg 100% betaald van de ov-kosten;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 vakantiedagen met de mogelijkheid om er 35 van te maken; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybride werken, vanuit huis, op kantoor (Rotterdam, Veenendaal) of zelfs tijdens je Workation; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EUR 65,- netto vitaliteitsbudget – we vinden het belangrijk dat we gezond blijven en een veilige werkplek hebben, zowel op kantoor als remote; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Je kunt deelnemen aan het leasefietsplan; &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;En vooral een leven lang leren. Op dag één start jouw onboardingprogramma, daarnaast krijg je een persoonlijk studiebudget dat je kunt inzetten voor jouw professionele ontwikkeling en ontvang je ook een GoodHabitz account, een online trainingstool voor je persoonlijke ontwikkeling.  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vrijheid, flexibiliteit en fun &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Je werkt in een internationale omgeving met professionals met verschillende nationaliteiten. Een flexibele werkweek van 40, 36 of 32 uur behoort tot de mogelijkheden omdat wij van mening zijn dat jouw manier van werken bij jouw levensstijl moet passen. HSO heeft professionals in dienst die plezier hebben in hun werk en klaar staan voor elkaar. Om het plezier in ons werk nog groter te maken, organiseren we uiteraard teamuitjes en bedrijfsfeesten, maar ook wekelijkse zomerborrels op ons dakterras, allerlei sportactiviteiten en is er de mogelijkheid bij te dragen aan onze Maatschappelijk Verantwoord Ondernemen-werkzaamheden.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Over HSO  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HSO is de eerste full-service Microsoft Partner in Nederland. Samen met ruim 2500 getalenteerde medewerkers in Europa, Azië en Noord-Amerika verlenen we ondersteuning op lokaal en internationaal niveau aan industriële bedrijven, retailers, financiële en zakelijke dienstverleners en overheidsinstellingen. &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HSO is voortdurend op zoek naar nieuw talent. We blijven onze wereldwijde community uitbreiden en scheppen er plezier in om samen te werken met prestatiegerichte mensen met een ondernemersgeest. Professionals die voortdurend willen leren en innoveren. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solliciteren &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enthousiast? Heb je vragen vooraf? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
